# MASTER PROJECT DEVELOPMENT PROMPT
## Academic Event and Resource Booking Portal — Complete MERN Full-Stack Application

Act as a **senior MERN stack developer, software architect, UI/UX designer, database designer, security engineer, and software testing specialist**.

Build a complete, production-style, fully functional MERN full-stack web application titled **“Academic Event and Resource Booking Portal.”**

The application must be suitable for a college final-year project review and demonstration. Do not create only a UI prototype, landing page, or frontend mockup. Develop the complete application with functional frontend, backend APIs, database integration, authentication, authorization, validation, booking conflict detection, admin controls, testing, and documentation.

## 1. Project Overview

**Project title:** Academic Event and Resource Booking Portal

**Problem statement:**
Educational institutions manage seminar halls, laboratories, classrooms, auditoriums, projectors, and other shared resources through manual registers, spreadsheets, emails, and messages. This leads to scheduling conflicts, double bookings, poor visibility of availability, delayed approvals, and inefficient resource utilization.

**Proposed solution:**
Develop a centralized web-based booking system that allows students, faculty members, and authorized staff to discover resources, check availability, submit booking requests, and track their requests. Administrators must be able to manage users, resources, events, approvals, booking schedules, and reports.

**Primary objective:**
Create a secure, responsive, attractive, and reliable booking platform that prevents overlapping reservations and provides separate dashboards for normal users and administrators.

