## 5. Core Booking Conflict Prevention Engine

This is the most important business requirement.

Implement a reliable server-side mechanism that prevents double bookings and overlapping reservations.

For example, if Seminar Hall A has an approved reservation from 10:00 AM to 12:00 PM, another request for the same hall from 11:00 AM to 1:00 PM must not be approved.

However, a reservation from 12:00 PM to 1:00 PM may be permitted if the institution does not configure a buffer period.

Use the half-open interval rule:

startA < endB AND endA > startB

Two reservations conflict when they refer to the same resource and their time intervals overlap.

Implement these rules:

1. Validate that the start time is before the end time.
2. Validate operating hours, maintenance periods, capacity, and booking restrictions.
3. Reject requests for dates in the past.
4. Prevent overlapping approved bookings for the same resource.
5. Recheck availability during administrative approval.
6. Recheck availability when a user edits a booking.
7. Ensure cancelled and rejected bookings do not block availability.
8. Prevent users from changing another user's bookings.
9. Return meaningful HTTP status codes and clear error messages.
10. Prevent race conditions when two requests attempt to reserve the same resource simultaneously.

Do not rely on a frontend availability check alone.

Implement transactional or atomic reservation handling appropriate to the chosen MongoDB deployment. If using MongoDB transactions, document the replica-set requirement. Ensure concurrent approvals cannot both succeed for overlapping time slots. Explain any limitations and how the implementation addresses them.

Support an optional configurable buffer time between reservations.

If two pending requests overlap, allow both to remain pending if appropriate, but ensure that only one can be approved for the conflicting time slot. Alternatively, implement a configurable temporary-hold policy and explain its expiration behavior.

Create automated tests for overlapping bookings, adjacent bookings, same-time requests, cancellations, maintenance periods, and concurrent approval attempts.

